<title>USA: Tight labor mkts in U.S warn of inflation - Minehan.</title>
<headline>Tight labor mkts in U.S warn of inflation - Minehan.</headline>
<dateline>MIDDLEBURY, Vermont 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Reserve Bank of Boston President Cathy Minehan said signs of tight U.S. labor markets are a warning of inflation.</p>
<p>&quot;These signals of labor market tightness in the face of above trend growth clearly sound inflation alarm bells,&quot; Minehan told a panel discussion on the economy at Middlebury College here.</p>
</text>
